+## Report evidence contract
 
-分析原则：
+不得套用固定分析流程、固定 section、圖表清單、順序或 caption。Choose the report story from the question and evidence, omitting irrelevant/empty sections. A requested dashboard remains a separately approved write, with publication confirmed later. These are evidence/schema dependencies, not an analysis workflow:
 
-- 必须把每个 selected view 放回整份报告脉络，说明它如何支持、修正或冲突于其他证据；不得用一份 artifact-level 说明取代多张 subpanel 的独立解读。
-- 数值与比较以 data model/facts 为准；PNG 只用于视觉形状与渲染观察。若两者冲突，以 model 为事实并标记图表问题。
-- 不能只写「相关非因果」「重要度非因果」等免责声明；要说明本图实际观察、为何重要、限制与下一步。
+- `prepare_ml_report(execution_ref, manifest_output_index)` supplies the opaque `report_context_ref` and bounded fact/artifact catalog. `inspect_report_artifacts` must cover all report artifacts in bounded batches, retaining each `inspection_ref`; selected views must be inspected. Current Ask O11y transport is text-only: use `mode=spec`, `visual_observation=null`, and never claim visual inspection. Browser rendering is a separate check.
+- After inspection, create 一次整份报告 synthesis with a cross-artifact thesis and `thesis_evidence`, not disconnected captions. Dynamically choose sections, relevant `view_ids`, order, titles, collapsed technical detail and optional `narrative_blocks`.
+- `ask-o11y-report-synthesis-v1` has exactly these top-level keys: `format`, `report_title`, `thesis`, `thesis_evidence`, `sections`. The dashboard `uid` and `title` are separate compose arguments, never legacy synthesis fields such as `purpose`.
+- Each selected panel/view follows the live schema: `artifact_id`, `view_ids`, `view_narratives`, `headline`, `data_observation`, `visual_observation`, `interpretation`, `limitation`, `next_step`, `evidence`. Provide independent per-view narratives in the whole-report context. Spec-only visual observations are null; do not add audience fields to the schema.
+- Numeric claims use deterministic `evidence: [{fact_ref, format}]`, not invented narrative numbers. Facts are authoritative; do not invent findings from graphics. If provided, a normalized operational summary may be explained using a business-appropriate denominator, never an automatic per-thousand template.
+- `compose_ml_dashboard(report_context_ref, inspection_refs, synthesis, ...)` validates evidence and returns opaque `refs.dashboard_ref`. Pass `{"dashboard": {"$dashboard_ref": "<refs.dashboard_ref>"}}` to the sole approved Grafana writer; do not copy full JSON or author asset URLs, raw Plotly data, datasource targets or scripts. Repair exact synthesis validation errors without rerunning completed analysis.
+- Plotly is the default analysis presentation: when charts or a dashboard are requested, emit sanitized Plotly figure artifacts and use `asko11y-plotly-panel` in `plotly` mode. Use `image` mode only for an explicit static-PNG request or an explicit `presentation_mode=image` tool argument. Text panels are narrative-only, never HTML/CSS/Markdown image workarounds. Invalid figures are errors, not silent fallbacks. Deterministic presentation supplies facts/artifacts, not the final story; fixture-only builders never belong in production.
